      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn linear word equations: costs, counts, rates and distribution.\n\nThis lesson uses the methods and question patterns from the Simplification chapter.\n\nWe will keep each step small: understand one rule, see it with numbers, then try a similar question.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Translate a cost story one item at a time.\n\nIf a pen costs p and a pencil costs q, then ‘3 pens and 2 pencils cost 80’ becomes 3p+2q=80.\n\nTwo independent statements give two equations.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
